  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A bar magnet with a magnetic moment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is placed in parallel position relative to a magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. The amount of required work done in turning the magnet form parallel to antiparallel position relative to the field direction is ________."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
